course: dictionary
lesson: 16183
title: Old words, old times
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Yore is an old word. It means long ago, a time far in the past. You will hardly ever hear it in everyday talk, but you will find it in stories, poems and fairy tales.
explain: Yore is nearly always in a phrase, such as "of yore". «Knights of yore rode across the land on their horses.» The phrase tells you the story is set in the old days, so the knights lived long ago.
explain: Look at the words around yore to check its meaning. Words like "long ago" and "old days" are clues. If you swap in "long ago" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Yore means long ago, or times long past.
fact: "Of yore" and "days of yore" both mean the old days.
fact: «Tales of yore» means stories from long ago.
fact: Yore is a noun, but you will almost only meet it inside a phrase like "of yore".
fact: Writers use yore to give a story an old-fashioned feel, like "Once upon a time".
exercise: What does yore mean? | Under the sea | Very loud | Next week | *Long ago
exercise: «In days of yore, the village had only one well.» What does "days of yore" mean? | Tomorrow and the days after | Days with lots of rain | Busy days at the seaside | *The old days, long past
exercise: Which phrase from a story means long ago? | every day | next summer | *of yore | right now
test: «Grandma tells tales of yore about her village.» What are the tales about? | Things sold in the shop today | Things happening this morning | Things that will happen next year | *Things that happened long ago
test: Where would you most likely find the word yore? | In a list of sums | On a shopping list | In a weather report | *In stories, poems and fairy tales
exam: «In days of yore, a dragon guarded the hills.» What do the words "in days of yore" tell you about the story? | It happens every Tuesday | It is about the weather today | *It happened long ago | It will happen tomorrow
